# Copy this file to `.env`. Expo inlines every EXPO_PUBLIC_* variable into the
# bundle, so nothing secret may ever live here — this address is public by
# design, which is exactly why the OpenAI key lives on the server instead.

# In development this must be this computer's LAN address, not localhost: the
# app runs on the phone, where localhost means the phone. Find it with
# `ipconfig` and take the IPv4 address of the adapter you are on.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.100.218:8080

# Google OAuth "Web client" id. Firebase console > Authentication > Sign-in
# method > enable Google — this auto-creates the client in Google Cloud
# Console under APIs & Services > Credentials, where you copy the id from.
#
# Sign-in with it does not work yet, on purpose: Google (and Apple) sign-in
# cannot run inside Expo Go at all — see the note in AccountScreen.tsx. This
# only becomes usable once the project moves to a development build (EAS
# Build / expo-dev-client), which is also when it needs a native Google
# Sign-In library, not the generic expo-auth-session OAuth flow this comment
# used to point at — that path (an auth.expo.io redirect) was deprecated by
# Expo years before SDK 54 and never worked here.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
